  "limitations": [
    "Published receipts require separate local byte-for-byte qualification before exactness is claimed",
    "Body bytes exclude HTTP headers, TLS, TCP/IP and tunnel overhead; packet evidence is joined separately",
    "Failed rows contain attempted upload body bytes and completely received response bodies, not proven link bytes",
    "No WAN speed claim follows from running this summarizer",
    "Break-even extrapolates constant per-transfer savings; it is not a measured sequence",
    "Receiver process CPU excludes relay/cloudflared and socket wait; sender CPU includes HTTP/TLS",
    "Failed pairs remain in receipts but are excluded from ratios; inspect failures before interpreting success-only statistics",
    "This shard has ten of thirty global paired trials; all three disjoint shards are required for the full campaign",
    "Every shard requires a fresh isolated receiver cache; its 960 MiB payload plus 240 KiB metadata allowance remains below 1 GiB",
    "Each arm has its own scope and an identically generated raw base seed; seed and transfer costs are reported separately and cumulatively",
    "Six arm permutations each occur five times over global trials 0..29; fixtures and ordering use the common campaign run ID",
    "The random 16 MiB fixture exceeds the DAG node cap: raw/zstd attempt bounded optional DAG warming before fallback, while sparse skips it; these are unequal CPU work paths",
    "No DAG/prepared arm or 64 MiB transport qualification is included",
    "Sparse comparison, encoding, identity hashes, HTTP exchange and terminal retained-state teardown are timed; fixture generation and reopened exact verification are separate",
    "Any Begin cache hit during a seed or modified-target upload invalidates the operation; all transfers have warm_probe=false",
    "Application cache state is controlled; OS page/disk caches, relay scheduling and thermal state are not controlled",
    "Receiver CPU covers decode/handle/encode; relay/cloudflared and socket waits are excluded; CPU is not energy",
    "HTTP body counts exclude packet/link overhead; failed-upload counts are attempted body bytes"
